<https://w3id.org/ssbd/EnvironmentalExternalitiesAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Assessment of environmental externalities."@en .
<https://w3id.org/ssbd/EnvironmentalExternalitiesAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "EnvironmentalExternalitiesAssessment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/ssbd/EnvironmentalExternalitiesAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Environmental Externalities Assessment is the formal procedure used to quantify and evaluate the uncompensated costs or benefits that economic activities impose on the environment. These costs are not often reflected in market prices, leading to misallocation of resources and distorted economic incentives. The assessment aims to internalise these overlooked environmental impacts."@en .
